WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:14.969
&gt;&gt;

00:00:14.989 --> 00:00:15.989
[Piano music playing]

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:20.899
Loic: Hi, my name is Loic Le Meur and I'm -- I've been based

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:21.919
in the

00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:24.899
Bay Area for about three years now.

00:00:24.919 --> 00:00:26.669
As you can tell, I'm French.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:28.189
I'm an interpreter.

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:30.959
I cannot fix my accent so I gave up fixing it.

00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:35.299
And I'm thrilled to be here so thank you for inviting me.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.339
I have creating a few startups in Europe and currently I'm

00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:39.359
doing two

00:00:39.359 --> 00:00:40.859
things probably like five stock tons.

00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:47.109
The first is seize me which is about bringing all the social

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:48.419
software

00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:51.289
that Scoble has talked about together because it's a real

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:52.579
pain to go

00:00:52.599 --> 00:00:55.599
and check all those places and share in all those places so

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:55.929
we're

00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:58.569
solving this very specific problem.

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:02.089
So we're on six platform so if you have an Android phone you

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.570
can try,

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.569
if you have a Blackberry you can try, iPhone that gets web

00:01:05.569 --> 00:01:07.329
everywhere.

00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:10.349
And the other thing I'm doing is a conference called "The

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:10.709
Web in

00:01:10.709 --> 00:01:13.459
Paris" which gathers two and a half thousand people from 50

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:16.909
countries -- lots of students, too -- and it became the

00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:17.929
largest tech

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:21.429
events in Europe, one of the top in the world, and we did it

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:21.869
with zero

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:22.869
marketing.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:24.189
Absolutely zero marketing.

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.530
All with social software.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:28.549
It started with 200 people, now we have two and a half

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:29.620
thousand and

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.590
every year I get people complain that I have not invited

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:33.890
them because

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:35.280
we don't invite anyone.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:38.299
We don't have any salesperson calling, we don't have any

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:38.479
marketing

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:39.479
material.

00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:40.339
Zero.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:40.729
Okay?

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:43.030
It does like $1.5 million in revenue every year.

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:44.049
Lethal business.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:46.780
Barely breaks even.

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:50.049
This is what I've been offered to talk about today is how

00:01:50.019 --> 00:01:51.019
the

00:01:51.019 --> 00:01:54.530
marketing is changing with social software and who in the

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:55.549
room would

00:01:55.549 --> 00:01:58.269
like to launch this business in the future?

00:01:58.289 --> 00:01:59.289
That's all?

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:00.289
Okay.

00:01:59.539 --> 00:01:59.739
&gt;&gt;

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:00.539
[Laughing]

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:02.879
Loic: Half of a room only?

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:04.649
Wow.

00:02:04.669 --> 00:02:05.669
Come on.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:06.009
You can do it.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:05.730
&gt;&gt;

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:06.530
[Laughing]

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:13.759
Loic: You know, I was at TED last week and James Cameron,

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.780
Avatar,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.499
right, and James said, you have the right to fail but you

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:21.519
never have

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:25.639
the right to fear something it was like that.

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:27.159
It'll come back to me.

00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:28.929
You shouldn't be scared of failure.

00:02:28.949 --> 00:02:31.769
You can fail but don't fear anything.

00:02:31.789 --> 00:02:33.029
Just try it.

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:35.049
So anyway, I'm going to constraint this.

00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:38.709
This is my blog and I've -- I've written this process today

00:02:38.729 --> 00:02:39.729
which is

00:02:39.729 --> 00:02:45.089
how I think marketing is changing and the rules that either

00:02:45.109 --> 00:02:46.109
startups

00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:49.909
or anything you do should follow to some extent and even

00:02:49.929 --> 00:02:50.929
large

00:02:50.929 --> 00:02:51.929
businesses.

00:02:51.179 --> 00:02:54.929
There are 22 of them and I have 15 minutes so I have to go

00:02:54.539 --> 00:02:55.539
really

00:02:55.539 --> 00:02:56.539
fast.

00:02:55.789 --> 00:02:59.039
This is why I wrote it if you want to find it again.

00:02:59.039 --> 00:03:02.039
But the first thing -- and I'm going to adapt it to

00:03:01.419 --> 00:03:02.419
entrepreneurship

00:03:02.419 --> 00:03:05.399
because you're interested in that -- I think the first thing

00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:06.419
you have

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.419
to do is not market research if you want to start a

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.189
business.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:14.099
Is really to identify an empty space which you think is

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.319
interesting

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.379
and just focus on that.

00:03:18.399 --> 00:03:21.529
Someplace where not that many people have created.

00:03:21.549 --> 00:03:25.029
So for example in location these days there is a lot

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:26.049
happening, like,

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:30.989
you know, Foursquare, and Gawala, and Google Latitude, like,

00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:32.009
saying

00:03:32.009 --> 00:03:34.019
where you are is something very new.

00:03:34.039 --> 00:03:37.289
Twitter is still, even though it's two and a half years old,

00:03:36.889 --> 00:03:37.889
a

00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:42.009
fantastic ecosystem which has a lot of empty space.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.280
By empty space I men a lot of spaces where you can create.

00:03:45.189 --> 00:03:49.469
So focus on that, find a niche, make it as small as possible

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:50.489
so that

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:53.239
you can be as good as possible in that niche.

00:03:53.259 --> 00:03:56.509
If you make it too wide, it's gonna be very risky because

00:03:56.139 --> 00:03:57.139
you -- it's

00:03:57.139 --> 00:03:59.889
difficult to be really good. So try to be really, really

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:00.810
good at

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.049
something very, very, very small.

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:06.929
Probably the best in the world as Seth Godin would say.

00:04:06.949 --> 00:04:07.949
Try to be that.

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:09.009
And then listen.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.529
So first rule is listen.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.039
Just so easy today.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:17.949
You use Twitter Search, you use Google Block Search, you use

00:04:17.969 --> 00:04:18.969
-- now

00:04:18.969 --> 00:04:22.019
Google has this realtime search and you just follow this

00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:23.199
space and see

00:04:23.219 --> 00:04:26.259
what people are doing and what people are saying about it.

00:04:26.279 --> 00:04:29.639
If your brand is not on quoted twitter these days it's

00:04:29.659 --> 00:04:31.319
either dead or

00:04:31.339 --> 00:04:32.589
it doesn't exist yet.

00:04:32.339 --> 00:04:37.480
I'd rather have people criticize heavily our brand than not

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.500
talk about

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.759
it at all because it's word of mouth and again these

00:04:41.779 --> 00:04:42.779
conferences that

00:04:42.779 --> 00:04:46.069
I take as example very often the web went from 200 people

00:04:46.089 --> 00:04:47.089
like a bunch

00:04:47.089 --> 00:04:50.220
of friends gathering six years ago into two and a half

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.370
thousand people

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:52.639
just from word of mouth.

00:04:52.649 --> 00:04:55.170
So you'd rather have word of mouth, even negative.

00:04:55.189 --> 00:04:58.670
We had a big crisis at the web when I invited politicians.

00:04:58.689 --> 00:05:01.439
We had two president the same day, Shimon Peres and the

00:05:00.769 --> 00:05:01.769
French

00:05:01.769 --> 00:05:04.769
President Nicolas Sarkozy, speak and that created a whole,

00:05:04.789 --> 00:05:05.789
you know,

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:08.230
controversy because bloggers didn't want to meet the

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.250
politicians that

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.500
much and the way I did it by imposing it and not telling

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:13.099
people before

00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:14.860
I created a huge mess.

00:05:14.879 --> 00:05:17.129
I had, like, the worst week of my life.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:20.509
Only criticism, you're burnt, you're never going to be able

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:21.529
to govern

00:05:21.529 --> 00:05:24.779
those people again, it's awful what you did to us, and it

00:05:24.349 --> 00:05:25.349
actually

00:05:25.349 --> 00:05:29.060
turned into a real huge positive for the conference because

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:30.079
I

00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:33.370
answered -- actually, Scoble advised me about on that --

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:34.389
every single

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:36.949
piece of piece of criticism.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.740
I listened to them all, I listened and answered every single

00:05:39.759 --> 00:05:40.759
one of

00:05:40.759 --> 00:05:43.509
them and then I said what I would do with it.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.079
So from probably not to impose politicians anymore to an

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:47.099
audience that

00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:48.349
was not prepared for that.

00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:50.569
That was a good lesson.

00:05:50.589 --> 00:05:53.339
You could have told me that before I'm sure; right?

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:53.889
Not to do that?

00:05:53.889 --> 00:05:57.360
Answer -- as I was saying, answer, answer, answer.

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:01.100
It looks very easy to say it but it's not that easy to

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.120
answer.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.089
Many brands listen but they don't engage.

00:06:05.109 --> 00:06:09.129
Many brands, as Robert said, Scott Monty at Ford or, you

00:06:09.149 --> 00:06:10.149
know,

00:06:10.149 --> 00:06:15.769
various -- there is Dell for example, Richard at Dell, and

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:16.789
Twitter.

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:20.259
You can follow those brands are answering all day long.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.829
And as I said, focus on the negative and start by this

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:24.849
first.

00:06:24.849 --> 00:06:26.349
It's a mark of attention.

00:06:26.099 --> 00:06:30.129
If people criticize you or your brand, sometimes insult you

00:06:30.149 --> 00:06:31.149
-- very

00:06:31.149 --> 00:06:32.149
often; right?

00:06:31.909 --> 00:06:34.269
It's awful what you read.

00:06:34.289 --> 00:06:35.289
That's okay.

00:06:35.289 --> 00:06:36.289
It's attention.

00:06:36.219 --> 00:06:37.469
It mean that is care.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.980
So, you know, answer and get to them.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.750
Of course you have to find a limit if it's a troll maybe you

00:06:42.589 --> 00:06:43.589
don't

00:06:43.589 --> 00:06:46.329
want to engage that much but -- and thank people.

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:50.019
If they say your brand rocks, if it's cool, just thank them.

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:51.289
Engage 24 hours a day.

00:06:51.149 --> 00:06:52.149
I'm sorry.

00:06:52.149 --> 00:06:53.149
This isn't big.

00:06:52.899 --> 00:06:54.899
Maybe we should have done slides after all.

00:06:54.899 --> 00:06:57.240
Anyway, engage 24 hours a day.

00:06:57.259 --> 00:07:01.360
The way we did it is we have two full-time community

00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:02.379
evangelists in

00:07:02.379 --> 00:07:08.259
San Francisco and one in Europe so that we can be 24 hours a

00:07:08.279 --> 00:07:09.350
day and

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.389
you could tell ho but we can't afford that.

00:07:12.409 --> 00:07:15.879
If you think about it, it is the budget of a PR agency.

00:07:15.899 --> 00:07:19.149
The monthly cost of a PR agency, you scratch that, I'm gonna

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:20.009
make new

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:25.560
friends today and cancel that, put it in full-time community

00:07:25.579 --> 00:07:28.240
evangelists who will listen and answer all day long.

00:07:28.259 --> 00:07:31.050
My goal is that anyone who says "Seesmic" on Twitter we

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:32.069
answer.

00:07:32.069 --> 00:07:34.069
Even if it's oh, that's great.

00:07:33.709 --> 00:07:35.120
We answer it.

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:36.889
That's what I want to do.

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:38.639
Very tough to do 24 hours a day.

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:41.889
I guarantee if you do that, you're going to have so much

00:07:41.609 --> 00:07:42.609
love and

00:07:42.609 --> 00:07:43.609
interaction.

00:07:42.859 --> 00:07:46.360
It's about a small quantity of people engaging with your

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:47.379
brands and

00:07:47.379 --> 00:07:48.560
not millions.

00:07:48.579 --> 00:07:53.360
Every single user that you make happy by answering will tell

00:07:53.379 --> 00:07:54.379
ten other

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:57.219
friends that Sees -- that your brand is cool.

00:07:57.239 --> 00:07:58.489
That's what we do.

00:07:57.889 --> 00:07:59.389
It worked very well for us.

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:03.829
That's our only market budget is word of mouth.

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:06.349
Be as transparent as possible -- I have to speed up.

00:08:06.329 --> 00:08:07.329
So don't cheat.

00:08:07.329 --> 00:08:10.079
If your product sucks, you have to recognize that it sucks.

00:08:09.849 --> 00:08:10.049
&gt;&gt;

00:08:10.049 --> 00:08:11.049
[Laughing]

00:08:10.049 --> 00:08:13.149
Loic: If --

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:13.369
&gt;&gt;

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:14.169
[Laughing]

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:15.419
Loic: If it's not complete, that's okay.

00:08:14.949 --> 00:08:19.459
People will forgive you for not being perfect but never

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:20.479
forgive you

00:08:20.479 --> 00:08:23.149
for cheating, for saying no, no, no.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.269
We put it under the carpet.

00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:28.039
Like, you know, the old style advertising when you used to

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:28.289
say

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:29.289
everything is fantastic; right?

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:30.629
This car has no problems.

00:08:30.649 --> 00:08:34.149
It's the best car in the world; and you never talk about the

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:33.879
negative.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:36.960
Sometimes actually talking ant the negatives in public as

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:37.980
you are the

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:41.230
CEO of that startup or if it's your project makes it even

00:08:41.059 --> 00:08:42.149
stronger

00:08:42.169 --> 00:08:44.850
because you recognize that it's a problem.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.870
So when you launch your startup, my advice is launch it as

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.490
fast as

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.990
possible, you know, throw yourself in the water and just

00:08:50.879 --> 00:08:51.879
start

00:08:51.879 --> 00:08:52.889
swimming.

00:08:52.909 --> 00:08:55.570
You will learn and iterate.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.590
Group for feedback.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.110
I'm going to show you how we do it.

00:08:59.129 --> 00:09:03.169
Good with feedback on a site like this which is here this

00:09:03.189 --> 00:09:04.189
one is

00:09:04.189 --> 00:09:05.189
yourethevoice.

00:09:05.179 --> 00:09:06.679
So we have so much feedback.

00:09:06.509 --> 00:09:09.759
We have a mention of Seesmic of every minute that we can't

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.230
really

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.230
tell.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.730
It's very difficult even though that's what I like to do.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:16.230
So what we do it's sort of a dig like.

00:09:15.639 --> 00:09:18.889
If you want to see, you know, our products so for example on

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:23.840
Seesmicweb, our web-based version, you have our users enter

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:24.860
feature

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:28.200
suggestions and ideas and they can put whatever they like

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.220
and then

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.889
people vote on them.

00:09:30.909 --> 00:09:33.659
So you can see for example we support twitter, whatever you

00:09:32.699 --> 00:09:33.699
want,

00:09:33.699 --> 00:09:37.509
facebook, one of the people wanted on that and we're

00:09:37.529 --> 00:09:38.559
building on just

00:09:38.579 --> 00:09:42.700
that right now; and so I call this my public road map.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.830
Public because anyone can see it, including the competition,

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.850
so you

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.850
know, you have to be careful of course.

00:09:48.689 --> 00:09:51.689
But say I want to see what people want on my Blackberry

00:09:51.449 --> 00:09:52.870
product I have

00:09:52.889 --> 00:09:53.889
that here.

00:09:53.649 --> 00:09:58.350
All our products have. a transparent feedback forum like

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.970
this and that

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:04.379
has been -- that has proven very, very useful for us.

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:07.389
So gather feedback on a feedback site like this.

00:10:07.409 --> 00:10:12.330
Very, very agile as you create the products.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:16.490
So one way we do it when we launch my company two years ago

00:10:16.509 --> 00:10:17.509
here, we

00:10:17.509 --> 00:10:20.009
launched it as -- I had this dream that everybody would

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:20.490
start talking

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.870
in video and that didn't happen yet.

00:10:22.889 --> 00:10:23.889
It will.

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:25.639
Trust me I'm sure it will.

00:10:25.389 --> 00:10:28.639
But we were too early and we didn't have enough traction so

00:10:28.039 --> 00:10:29.039
we changed

00:10:29.039 --> 00:10:32.149
everything into what our company's doing now.

00:10:32.169 --> 00:10:33.480
You have to be agile.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.659
If it doesn't work, just change and move the space into

00:10:36.679 --> 00:10:37.679
something that

00:10:37.679 --> 00:10:39.429
has more traction.

00:10:39.449 --> 00:10:42.439
So change your priorities often based on this public road

00:10:42.459 --> 00:10:43.459
map that

00:10:43.459 --> 00:10:46.480
I've shown you and keep moving.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.750
You have to be very, very agile with this.

00:10:48.679 --> 00:10:49.929
Don't forget to innovate.

00:10:49.789 --> 00:10:53.500
Scoble said, if a Porsche -- if Porsche had listened to its

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:54.519
users, it

00:10:54.519 --> 00:10:57.569
would become a Volvo because if you got a big trunk.

00:10:57.589 --> 00:11:00.059
And so listening to the users is not enough.

00:11:00.079 --> 00:11:03.590
You also have to innovate, create things, the empty space

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:04.610
that wasn't

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.649
created before, you have to create a presence on the most

00:11:07.669 --> 00:11:08.669
popular

00:11:08.669 --> 00:11:10.819
social software, all of them.

00:11:10.839 --> 00:11:14.339
You have no idea -- maybe you have but I had no idea on how

00:11:14.089 --> 00:11:15.089
many

00:11:15.089 --> 00:11:18.500
interactions I would get different in Linkdin than on

00:11:18.519 --> 00:11:19.519
Twitter or

00:11:19.519 --> 00:11:20.519
facebook.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.490
They are not the same people.

00:11:21.429 --> 00:11:23.100
You think they are the same.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.370
They are not the same.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.370
I am not getting at all the same level of interaction with

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.740
Linkdin.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.080
The way you do it is two ways.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.860
Either you adapt the message to people or you just, uh,

00:11:33.879 --> 00:11:34.879
publish the

00:11:34.879 --> 00:11:38.090
same which I decided to do and actually acquired a little

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.110
very cool

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:41.830
service called PFN to just help you do that, share

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:42.850
everywhere at the

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:43.850
same time.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.600
You have to be everywhere.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:46.460
You have to identify your best fans.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.840
It's not ant getting a million fans like MC Hammer.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:56.229
It's about getting the first --

00:11:56.249 --> 00:11:56.449
&gt;&gt;

00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:57.449
[Laughing]

00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:57.699
Loic: I mean, we all --

00:11:57.539 --> 00:11:57.740
&gt;&gt;

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:58.740
[Laughing]

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:01.659
Loic: We all dream about that; right?

00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:04.679
But it's -- at the beginning it's about -- I'm actually

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.610
quoting

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:05.610
Hammer.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:07.360
He knows that for an hour ago he said that.

00:12:07.299 --> 00:12:10.949
But you have to start with a hundred people, then 200 very

00:12:10.969 --> 00:12:11.969
committed

00:12:11.969 --> 00:12:13.730
fans, you have to focus on those.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:17.299
I really advise you to read Seth Godin's book, "Tribes".

00:12:17.319 --> 00:12:20.949
He quotes actually someone else saying a thousand fans can

00:12:20.969 --> 00:12:21.969
get the

00:12:21.969 --> 00:12:25.199
word out to millions and you really have to focus on the

00:12:25.219 --> 00:12:26.219
small group.

00:12:26.219 --> 00:12:29.009
When you do create focus on the very small social network

00:12:29.029 --> 00:12:30.029
that you

00:12:30.029 --> 00:12:32.779
could create for them like we did, we have these thousand

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:33.750
fans on

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.750
Seesmic.

00:12:34.649 --> 00:12:37.399
It's a Ning social network called Team Seesmic where we

00:12:37.019 --> 00:12:38.019
gather them

00:12:38.019 --> 00:12:41.199
all and we give them exclusives, we can give them products

00:12:41.219 --> 00:12:42.219
before

00:12:42.219 --> 00:12:44.759
anyone else and I think they like it.

00:12:44.779 --> 00:12:46.179
Love your users.

00:12:46.199 --> 00:12:49.620
I did something very bad to our office managers two weeks

00:12:49.639 --> 00:12:50.639
ago.

00:12:50.639 --> 00:12:53.639
I said, who wants some stickers, and we have, like, 50,000

00:12:53.449 --> 00:12:54.449
followers

00:12:54.449 --> 00:12:58.730
on twitter and we received 500 e-mails in an hour of fans

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.750
who wanted

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.139
stickers of, you know, of a raccoon which is there on my

00:13:03.159 --> 00:13:04.740
computer and

00:13:04.759 --> 00:13:07.610
of course we sent every single -- so she loved me.

00:13:07.629 --> 00:13:10.629
For about a week she was sending stickers and then we found

00:13:10.179 --> 00:13:11.179
a company

00:13:11.179 --> 00:13:12.179
that.

00:13:11.429 --> 00:13:16.279
But now we have a Seesmic sticker on a snow board, you know,

00:13:16.299 --> 00:13:17.299
people

00:13:17.299 --> 00:13:20.620
tweet the picture so it's very good love around you.

00:13:20.639 --> 00:13:21.889
And I'm almost done.

00:13:21.649 --> 00:13:24.279
You have to be everywhere and on every platform.

00:13:24.299 --> 00:13:26.799
And I'm talking about your brand, your company here.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.360
Very tough.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.860
You have to be on the web, you have to be on the iPhone,

00:13:30.459 --> 00:13:31.459
now, too, you

00:13:31.459 --> 00:13:34.959
have to have an Android app, you have to have a Nokia app to

00:13:34.459 --> 00:13:35.459
reach the

00:13:35.459 --> 00:13:39.500
2 million users that still Nokia has between Europe and Asia

00:13:39.519 --> 00:13:40.519
and not

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:43.769
so much in fact U.S., you have to have a Blackberry app.

00:13:43.199 --> 00:13:44.449
So it's a nightmare.

00:13:44.199 --> 00:13:47.110
As a developer, it's horrible because these are all

00:13:47.129 --> 00:13:48.199
difficult bases.

00:13:48.219 --> 00:13:49.469
But that's our goal.

00:13:49.219 --> 00:13:52.219
There are some companies that can help you do that but if

00:13:51.969 --> 00:13:52.969
you have a

00:13:52.969 --> 00:13:55.340
cool brand you should probably think about being everywhere.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.819
And I'm almost done.

00:13:56.839 --> 00:13:59.909
You need to use social networking internally if you want to

00:13:59.929 --> 00:14:00.929
get

00:14:00.929 --> 00:14:01.929
familiar with it.

00:14:01.679 --> 00:14:04.929
Sales force is doing a whole thing with that.

00:14:04.949 --> 00:14:08.429
You have to participate in all the cool events that all the

00:14:08.449 --> 00:14:09.449
social

00:14:09.449 --> 00:14:15.350
networking junkies like Scoble, go to, Southwest, you know,

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.209
Leaf, DLD,

00:14:17.229 --> 00:14:18.610
web, tech50, and so on.

00:14:18.629 --> 00:14:22.439
Go there and meet them even if you're not a geek brand.

00:14:22.459 --> 00:14:26.500
You have to have real people in front of those brands

00:14:26.519 --> 00:14:27.519
because it's

00:14:27.519 --> 00:14:29.019
like it's not about Ford.

00:14:28.769 --> 00:14:30.769
It's more ant who answers at Ford.

00:14:30.599 --> 00:14:33.639
We want to have a human relationship.

00:14:33.659 --> 00:14:35.610
And few little things.

00:14:35.629 --> 00:14:39.299
Use video, very good as Robert knows, of course; be

00:14:39.319 --> 00:14:40.319
proactive and

00:14:40.319 --> 00:14:41.819
share as much as you can.

00:14:41.819 --> 00:14:44.819
Think about we're gonna have coffee, what do we talk about,

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.000
or have

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.909
lunch, what do we talk about?

00:14:46.929 --> 00:14:49.909
Don't think about what should be my next press release

00:14:49.929 --> 00:14:50.929
because that's

00:14:50.929 --> 00:14:52.389
going to be very boring.

00:14:52.409 --> 00:14:55.659
If I, you know, have coffee with you and I only talk about

00:14:55.169 --> 00:14:56.169
in terms

00:14:56.169 --> 00:14:58.669
marketing, press release, it is going to be super boring.

00:14:58.669 --> 00:15:01.919
I want to know about you and companies start to have a human

00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:02.279
voice.

00:15:02.279 --> 00:15:04.959
Last point: Passions.

00:15:04.979 --> 00:15:06.449
It takes years.

00:15:06.469 --> 00:15:07.779
It doesn't take days.

00:15:07.799 --> 00:15:09.179
It take years.

00:15:09.199 --> 00:15:11.209
It doesn't take months either.

00:15:11.229 --> 00:15:14.750
Building trust around yourself helps as brands or around

00:15:14.769 --> 00:15:15.769
your company

00:15:15.769 --> 00:15:16.799
takes years.

00:15:16.819 --> 00:15:20.069
It's a very long process but then it's extremely useful for

00:15:19.669 --> 00:15:20.669
doing

00:15:20.669 --> 00:15:23.340
good, for helping others, and if you focus on helping

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.360
others, even

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.110
though you're a profit-oriented business, it's probably a

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:27.959
good -- a

00:15:27.959 --> 00:15:28.959
good rule.

00:15:28.459 --> 00:15:30.209
So anyway, that was my 22-cents.

00:15:29.959 --> 00:15:33.379
Thank you very much.

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:33.600
&gt;&gt;

00:15:32.399 --> 00:15:33.399
[Applause]

